# Goal supervisor reviewer credential (RUNBOOK 7.16) — optional.
#
# The reviewer only needs this when nobody wants to log the box into grok
# interactively. `grok login --device-code` (one browser approval, then the
# session token refreshes itself) is the alternative; an XAI_API_KEY from
# console.x.ai is the documented no-browser path and is the one used when the
# isolated GROK_HOME has no auth.json.
#
# The real file lives ONLY at ~/.config/remote-agent/grok.env, mode 0600, and is
# never committed. The supervisor reads exactly the names below and passes only
# those into the reviewer's environment — nothing else from this file, and
# nothing from the unit's own environment.
#
# Precedence trap: a session token in the same GROK_HOME wins over the key
# (resolution order: model api_key > env_key > session token > XAI_API_KEY), so
# use one method per home. `grok logout`/deleting auth.json falls back to the key.

XAI_API_KEY=
